    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d221">

                <pb facs="0283" n="249" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg249"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote to Mr. Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-03-30"><hi rendition="#italic">March 30,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have been requested to
                    inquire, unofficially, whether it is the intention of the President of the
                    United States to send a special mission of congratulation on the occasion of the
                    celebration, in June next, of the sixtieth anniversary of the Queen’s accession
                    to the throne.</p>
                <p>I should be greatly obliged if you could enable me to give Lord Salisbury the
                    information desired.</p>
                <p>I remain, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
